    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change mirrors the established pattern in `OwnerMapper` exactly. `formatSelfLink` sits among the sibling `format*` helpers (e.g. `formatDisplayName`, `formatSalutation`), carries the same style of Javadoc, uses the same `owner == null || owner.getId() == null` null-guard idiom used by peers like `formatCheckDigit`/`formatMembershipNumber`, and is wired via `@Mapping(..., expression = \"java(formatSelfLink(owner))\")` identically to the other derived fields. The OpenAPI `selfLink` schema entry matches the surrounding `readOnly` field conventions. Logic is in the right unit (the mapper that owns DTO derivation), nothing is duplicated, and the interface is not being overloaded with unrelated responsibilities beyond what it already does.",
